{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1075386-looking-for-a-mage-skype-game","id":1075386,"title":"Looking for a Mage skype game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-08T23:46:01-07:00","id":1075386,"title":"Looking for a Mage skype game","content":"The title basically explains it. Pbp just fall apart far too easily. I find that a good first few sessions in real time can launch a game so much farther forward than several months of play by post can. This in turn breathes a lot of life into the interest of the game.<br /> <br /> So, that being said, I would like to be one of the players. I don't feel comfortable enough with running a game myself, and I'm itching to figure out mysteries during game play.<br /> <br /> I would like the setting to be Salamanca Spain, as the central mystery to that location is very intriguing to me (this is negotiable).<br /> <br /> I would personally like to play a Mystogogue Mastigos. The Mastigos path is of large interest to me, while the Mysterium interests me in that they have their very own mystery that they engage in (the atlantean mystery, wherein you acquire ability within the egregore).<br /> <br /> I'd like to keep horror somewhat on the down low. I'm not so much referring to personal horror where you make decisions and have to deal with the fall out of how you use your magic and mundane skills (that's a central theme to Mage, after all), but rather less gore and monsters, if you will. I wouldn't mind a touch of crossover from the other splats (especially changeling), but in general I think it would be best if we stuck to Mage, as far as that goes.<br /> <br /> It would be really nice if the merits from the spoiled portions of Signs of Sorcery to be available. And in that same vein, there is a list of home brewed merits on these forums. I would take it as a personal favor if the storyteller at least looked through that list, if not actually allowed any of them.<br /> <br /> I'd like there the be a player limit of 5, with a preference towards 2, 3, or 4. Fewer players means the storyteller can get into more personal quests for the players' characters, which is sometimes either critical or very desirable. Just to note, if there's no other player interest, I would not be completely opposed to a solo game.<br /> <br /> Currently I work third shift on an eastern standard time zone, so I'm really only available late, late Friday's or on Saturdays. Some Saturdays I would not be available, and I'm sure that others will have times when they cannot meet as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, to drum up a bit of interest, here's a couple of questions: What are your three most favorite spells in 2ed, and why?<br /> <br /> Mine are Teleportation, Alter Direction, and Augment Mind. The first spell is the iconic poster boy for Space magic, and the fact that you can now teleport things between two locations without actually being there is amazing. The second spell sums up some of the awesomeness that is now Space magic; Alter Direction is capable of doing so many different things based upon the scenario and spell factors. Finally, Augment Mind is the Mind spell I would most want to be able to have in real life if magic were real; the ability to increase how fast my mind works, or to increase my natural charisma, or even to just become more resolved would be absolutely fantastic!<br /> <br /> So! Anyone interested in storytelling or playing a 2ed Mage the Awakening game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:26:52-07:00","id":1075762,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd love to play! Only thing missing is an ST it seems. If anyone would ST, I'd bring Ignis, my Obrimos Mystagogue and his Familiar, Hoarfrost. Ignis works in an occult shop and is an alchemist with an affinity for the 4 elements (Forces 3, Matter 2, Prime 1).<br /> My favorite spells from 2e would possibly be Shaping (oh the joy of DIY things coming out perfect!!!), Discern Composition (as a geologist it would save me a lot of headaches) and basically the entire Forces Arcanum (control over electronic equipment and the forces of Nature including but not restricted to: weather, fire, temperature and being able to fly and be invisible? WHERE DO I SIGN?!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T03:51:26-07:00","id":1075827,"title":"","content":"Hehehe! I love to see that enthusiasm!<br /> <br /> Also, it's nice to see another fellow mystagogue! Having two players in that order makes doing internal affairs much more interesting.<br /> <br /> As to alchemist...how do you mean? My understanding of alchemy in Mage is that it's basically the Matter arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:31:09-07:00","id":1075905,"title":"","content":"Well, that's basically it. He's an Obrimos who dabs in Matter, his Obsession being the perfection of Nature, his Hubris being to control it. Working in an occult shop, he sometimes empowers the ingredients just a tad bit so, making incense more fragrant, infusions more potent, the crystals more limpid. That's why he's an alchemist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:54:16-07:00","id":1076165,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I just have seen other people talk about alchemy as if they were talking about potions or other cool, non Mage magic. The way you said he was an alchemist without him being a Moros made me think you might have meant something like that. That's why I was looking for clarification.<br /> <br /> In any case, yeah, we just need a storyteller now.<br /> <br /> As to my character, I was actually thinking of tying his awakening into the main mystery at Salamanca. Like, he'd been a decent businessman before and had been on a vacation with his girlfriend and her family. Unknown to him his girlfriend's family was a proximus dynasty run by the silver ladder and his girlfriend was actually a mage herself. Her father starts to think that my character will not awaken, so the girlfriend takes drastic action and brings the character along through a portal to another world. He awakens during the process, but only he returns when the portal collapses, which of course doesn't follow the norm for that mystery. <br /> <br /> Something like that, anyways. It can be changed if that isn't the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T06:58:50-07:00","id":1076454,"title":"","content":"The character I'm envisioning would have an obsession with irises and portal magic (emphasis on Space), and would be hubristic (i.e. apathetic) about the connections formed to create and explore such magic.<br /> <br /> So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11807_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11807\" data-vbnamecard=\"11807\">HTaiji</a>, out of curiosity, what made you want to go with Obrimos over Moros? I'm with you there, I personally prefer the Obrimos path over the Moros myself, but given that the alchemist is one of the achetypes of the Moros, its an interesting twist to see an Obrimos pursuing that archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:45:04-07:00","id":1076582,"title":"","content":"Forces and Prime. Ignis is a guy who Awoke during a time of revelation, meditating over a fire, communing with the Elements. His Path became Obrimos because he really isn't about the experience of alchemy, studying it for its sake. No, he uses it as a tool to shape the world around him, to be in control of Nature around him, just as he controls the skies, the winds, light, heat, flame and lightning itself. Obrimos being the Path of the Mighty, and him wanting control, made the most sense. He'd then learn Matter to be able to more closely manipulate the other elemental manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T03:04:17-07:00","id":1076880,"title":"","content":"Ah. I see. Makes sense. It's a natural complement to his Forces focus. Interestingly enough, I feel the same way about Life and both Mind and Space. Life magic is a natural complement to Mind magic, combining to give perfect control of both the body and mind. It also helps a Space mage handle some of the crazy crap one can get into by all that exploration they tend to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:53:18-07:00","id":1076941,"title":"","content":"I would like to play a fortune teller, a very accurate but not perfect fortune teller. A male fortuneteller, you don't get many of those. as an Acanthus I would be Fate 3 Time 2 and Space 1 as an elective. He is black, though he grew up with and was trained by the Roma, awakened ones. I believe that they were the roaming fortunetellers and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 04-12-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:03:24-07:00","id":1077112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1067793-looking-for-players\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1067793-looking-for-players\"> Looking for players. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1067793-looking-for-players\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1067793-looking-for-players </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hey. I plan on hosting a Mage 2e Oneshot on the NERDHerd Discord servers tomorrow at 2 pm EST after our streamed dnd game. I've got a couple people in our group already interested but I need at least one more person to round the group out. I plan on using the MythicGM Emulator to replace the ST function, but it's okay if you're not familiar with it. You can hit me up tonight via PM if you're interested so we can talk about characters and some of the requirements a character needs to meet to mesh well with the MythicGM. While I plan on this being a oneshot that's mostly because I don't have the </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Discord instead of Skype, but hey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:50:07-07:00","id":1077240,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> : Aye, it doesn't strictly have to be skype, but this weekend doesn't look good for me. And while I am craving some mage, one of the things I like most about these rpgs is the ability to see long term progress in both character development and story development. Thanks for the offer though. If this weekend did work out for me I'd definitely try to join in.<br /> <br /> Also, welcome <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a>. Having an Acanthus would help to make the cabal a little bit more well rounded, so great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:58:16-07:00","id":1077244,"title":"","content":"Well, I plan on letting characters achieve long term progress, I'm just staging it as oneshots because I don't plan on running them regularly and I expect that I'll have players like you that drop in and out depending on my infrequent schedule. Maybe next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:45:15-07:00","id":1077336,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, I'd love to join y'all! Unfortunately, I'm not comfortable STing but playing in a low-horror Chronicles of Darkness game sounds like a dream. Ideally I'd like to play an Obrimos university student focusing on Prime and Mind. If y'all are wanting an all Mystagogue game then I'd be happy to play along. If you'd prefer diversity, I am just as happy playing a Libertine.<br /> As to your question, my three favorite spells in order are:<br /> #1, Psychic Genesis, especially in combination w/ life, prime or matter 5, because creating a brand new being ex-nihilo is an awesome capstone ability.<br /> #2, Words of Truth, because it's just plain cool.<br /> #3, Transform Life, because who doesn't want to become a tentacle monster? (This is perfectly innocent; get your head out out of the gutter, lol.)<br /> <br /> I'm also in eastern time, and I'm available on Friday nights but I'm already in a skype Exalted game that happens on Saturday afternoons. I don't mind playing two games on Saturdays but the scheduling might be difficult.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:39:55-07:00","id":1077587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1075386-looking-for-a-mage-skype-game?p=1077244#post1077244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I plan on letting characters achieve long term progress, I'm just staging it as oneshots because I don't plan on running them regularly and I expect that I'll have players like you that drop in and out depending on my infrequent schedule. Maybe next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. It's unfortunate then that my schedule doesn't work out this coming Saturday. I'll keep it in mind come your next one shot.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1081_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1081\" data-vbnamecard=\"1081\">Fictional Dynasty</a> : welcome! An all mystagogue group would definitely be interesting. Four new mages to a concilium that join together as a cabal and all join the same order would give that order a pretty decent bump in political power, among other things. And don't worry about possibly doubling down on paths, it seems that your character's concept and Taiji's are different.<br /> <br /> Well, that's four players that are interested. I wonder if we can get a St to join in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 04-13-2017, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:50:45-07:00","id":1077595,"title":"","content":"For when a group doesn't have an ST I advocate for MythicGM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:08:06-07:00","id":1077832,"title":"","content":"I've never used MythicGM so I don't know how well it works. It does seem like a last resort though. What do y'all say to waiting for at least a week to see if we can find a storyteller? If we can't find one then we could meet on Friday the 21st and try MythicGM. Does that sound good to everyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:20:46-07:00","id":1077922,"title":"","content":"We have already done one game with the Mystic GM and it does leave alot to desire. It is ok and it can throw alot of twist in there. I can see where it would be a good ST tool. It went well enough that I will be back for the next one and so I guess that is saying something. I am a very structured player and ST and this does lack structure. But as I said it went ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:45:26-07:00","id":1077932,"title":"","content":"Hmm, it does seem like MythicGM could possibly work, though it is obviously a lot less desirable than a full ST. As to meeting times, I'd like to clarify that I would not be available until after 10:00 p.m. on Fridays, though around 6 on Saturdays. Given I work 3rd shift right now I could stay up long after that, but I doubt most people want to start that late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 04-13-2017, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:37:10-07:00","id":1078042,"title":"","content":"For the MythicGM thing, the more stuff you create to be input into it in terms of NPCs and possible plot threads the better it will function. It also requires the people using it to be willing to jump in and interpret its results. I can promise that eventually, it will hit everything you want it to because that's it's function, and with full player participation it will do it in ways that should satisfy the participants. A good ST is a person with a compelling vision, but on the other hand a group of people willing to brainstorm an idea is a viable development method for a reason. You're essentially crowd sourcing your story that -you- want instead of putting the whole burden on one person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:39:07-07:00","id":1078043,"title":"","content":"As I am UST Saturday would work better for me... 10pm there is 3am here, and while I can stay awake until 6am without a problem, it would be more enjoyable for me if it would start at 6pm (that's 11pm here) and Saturday means I no longer have my head clogged with teacher stuff xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:41:07-07:00","id":1078079,"title":"","content":"Can we state the times in GMT as that is universal to all, As i am -7 GMT and East Coast is -4 GMT I have no idea what UST is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:19:28-07:00","id":1078108,"title":"","content":"UST is GMT if I'm not mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:29:28-07:00","id":1078113,"title":"","content":"Sorry, that was supposed to be UCT or Universal Coordinated Time, phone corrected to UST for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:33:07-07:00","id":1078114,"title":"","content":"Ok I know what UCT is I was confused with UST, That is why GMT is bets as an indicator. UCT being the same thing would also work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:49:18-07:00","id":1078124,"title":"","content":"My Other game starts at 5pm EDT(9pm UCT) every other Saturday. So for me to make it, our game has to be either, later that night, or start around noon(4pm UTC) or earlier on Saturdays, or once every two weeks when I don't have a game.@Falcon777 How early can you wake up on Saturdays?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T00:06:55-07:00","id":1078200,"title":"","content":"I can get up as early as 3 pm est (11 gmt?) on saturdays, possibly 2, though that'd be pushing it<br /> I'd also need at least 30 minutes from then just to wake up.<br /> <br /> I would be ok with meeting every two weeks, though, if everyone else is ok with it.<br /> <br /> As to mythicgm, I think the largest deficiency it might have for mage 2e is aiding us in creating mysteries. It seems like it could do villians decently, but mysteries are almost by definition opposite of what it seems it can do. We'll have to figure that one out somehow, perhaps have a rotating roster of who is creating the mystery of the day.<br /> <br /> Also, welcome <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T03:21:13-07:00","id":1078253,"title":"","content":"Easter is only GMT -4 so 3 pm eastern is 7pm GMT and noon pacific.<br /> <br /> I would have to agree with the mysteries part of this. The real strength of MysticGM is to take the decision making process to a chaotic level. For instance one of the players asked if his mentor was a (Arrow, Guardian, FC, Ladder, Mysterium) and all the answers was no for each one he asked about but was a yes for Seer. So his mentor is a hidden Seer. I think that is great and that kind of Chaos in the mix can really shake things up. I asked if the person that helped him get off the streets as a child was a mage and it said yes. I did not expect this and my backstory didn't account for this but it is now there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T03:39:24-07:00","id":1078260,"title":"","content":"BTW I am close to finishing the setting for a game of Mage the will be located in Phoenix Arizona (Where I live) I have been an ST for many years, although it has been for oWoD, This will be my first CofD game as the ST. I have several options at my disposal to use as the ST. The one that I would probably use would be to run it on Discord (If I can figure out all of the stuff needed, like how to keep some stuff secrete and everything). The second option is a VTT (Virtual Tabletop, for those unfamiliar with what VTT means) My preferred VTT is Fantasy Grounds. I have the full package and can host games. When I am ready I will discuss it with the players as to their prefers method of playing in a game.<br /> <br /> What this boils down to is if we can come up with a good time for everyone then I may be starting a game soon. I am in the MST time zone (Always -7 GMT, no daylight saving time shift) at the moment I am -3 EDT (Equal to PDT) I work from 0400 - 1330 (1100 - 2030 GMT) Monday through Friday, with every other Friday off, so most evenings and all Saturdays are free. I have a Face-to-Face group every other Sunday so I would prefer no Sundays but if Sunday is the only time then it would be the opposite Sunday from my Face-to-Face game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T03:51:12-07:00","id":1078261,"title":"","content":"Oh, wow! An offer for a St. That's great!<br /> <br /> As to the program we use to communicate, so long as it is real time and fairly well known I'm good with it. It'd be best if we could at least get audio from everyone.<br /> <br /> As to my availability, I work Sunday night through Thursday night from 7:00 p.m est (or 11:00 pm gmt?) to 4 a.m. est (or 8 gmt?). My housemates and I hold house meetings every other Friday after I get back from my small group at church, so those Fridays would be a no go. Anyways, I wouldn't be able to start until about 10:00 p.m. est (2.00 a.m. gmt?) on Fridays where there wasn't a house meeting. Saturdays, however, I should be available from 4 pm est (8pm gmt?) to late into the night and early morning (so long as I wasn't visiting my family).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:00:37-07:00","id":1078292,"title":"","content":"The offer for ST is provided that I can get everything set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:20:25-07:00","id":1078299,"title":"","content":"Please excuse my denseness and bear with me. The game is to be played at what time Eastern Standard Time on Saturday?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:25:41-07:00","id":1078301,"title":"","content":"It sounds like everyone is available every other Saturday afternoon(EDT) if that works for you wtaylorjr2001?<br /> <br /> p.s. Yay a gm! Thank you Hardwire99!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","user":"Fictional Dynasty","date":". 04-14-2017, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:58:35-07:00","id":1078314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1075386-looking-for-a-mage-skype-game?p=1078292#post1078292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The offer for ST is provided that I can get everything set up.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is anything I can do that would assist you, please let me know. I'd be happy to create a small cabal of npc mages, or a small group of sleepwalkers. <br /> <br /> And yes, I'm having a very hard time falling asleep atm. I should have been asleep 3 hours ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:04:45-07:00","id":1078322,"title":"","content":"At this moment I am asking you to provide the time you would be available. After everyone have provided their possible time then we can decide as a group the best time that would accommodate everyone.<br /> <br /> BTW and little insight into my personality. I am a very structured person. I like my plans and like others to have plans. I also realize that it doesn't always work out that well. I am also detail oriented and sometime overload with detail. Documentation is also very important. Being an engineer I ask why alot so please excuse me if I ask alot of questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T10:25:13-07:00","id":1078415,"title":"","content":"My schedule is mostly pretty flexible. Other than the game every other Saturday I'm usually very busy Sunday through Tuesday. Any other time is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:03:30-07:00","id":1078454,"title":"","content":"12 in the afternoon on Saturday is fine for me. 12 EDT is 12 EST so its good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:18:06-07:00","id":1078463,"title":"","content":"It would have to be late afternoon for Falcon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:40:35-07:00","id":1078478,"title":"","content":"I'm good from 10 EST till about 22 EST (that's 15h GMT to 03h GMT) on Saturdays. Hardwire, no problems about getting asked &quot;why&quot; it's basically my job. Would you want us to send you a character sheet with background story? As for system, Roll20 also supports CofD with character sheets and dice rollers, and it's also free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:49:51-07:00","id":1078483,"title":"","content":"Barring foobars I can do any time on Saturdays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:01:43-07:00","id":1078490,"title":"","content":"So does 4pm EDT(8pm UCT) every other week, starting next week, work for everyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:09:13-07:00","id":1078493,"title":"","content":"I will not be ready by next week to start the Chronicle. I will ask everyone to submit character sheets when I start the game. You can start planning the Cabal/Characters before I start and I was looking at starting characters +20 experience. So plan what you will I will let you know when I am ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:47:38-07:00","id":1078514,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> since my character will own an occult shop, would you want in and be the resident fortune teller? :P<br /> As for the +20xp given, what do you guys think about spending 2xp each for a dot in Safe Space and another in Sanctum? The Sanctum can be in the basement with a suite of apartments above, one for each member of the cabal. If you want me to, I can draw a rough plan of the building.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> do you have an idea in which city will the Chronicle take place? So I can start looking at buildings xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:56:35-07:00","id":1078517,"title":"","content":"Phoenix Arizona where I live so that I can pay attention to the story instead of trying to learn about a City also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:59:24-07:00","id":1078521,"title":"","content":"Phoenix Metropolitan Area is a little over 16,000 square miles build in a desert, Lots of places to have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T14:50:03-07:00","id":1078547,"title":"","content":"I agree w/ spending two points each divided between safe space and sanctum. Are we doing an all Mysterium cabal or are we going to be mixing it up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:04:55-07:00","id":1078559,"title":"","content":"Two of us will be Mysterium at least, me and Falcon777, but I see no reason to have either or. I think it would be interesting having a full Mysterium cabal, and like wise a mixed cabal would also be fun, so choose whichever makes more sense for your char, I guess :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:06:04-07:00","id":1078560,"title":"","content":"The safe space/sanctum bit is a great idea. That being said, I will probably flavor the safe space dot as a spell my character has cast. <br /> <br /> My character will be in the Mysterium, others are welcome to choose what they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:12:13-07:00","id":1078567,"title":"","content":"I vote Mysterium. My favorite spells are Shifting the Odds, Perfect Timing, and and Ground Eater. He is a very lucky man, moving and acting at the perfect time and very good at running for his life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:35:17-07:00","id":1078587,"title":"","content":"BTW just so that you don't go hog wild with the 20 exp, I like balanced characters, no starting out as a master or with a Gnosis of more than four. I also know that alot of people like to use fate because that don't spend alot of points on merits and they can overload a skill and shift the points when needed. You will find I allow that but there are alot of ways that will hamper that practice, so be forewarned that it is still a good idea to spend hard points on merits and spread your skill points around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:59:10-07:00","id":1078604,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7825\" data-vbnamecard=\"7825\">Falcon777</a> a &quot;Ward&quot; spell cast on the Sanctum/Safe Place is a perfect way of doing that. I might flavor mine as a &quot;Wards and Signs&quot; on top of that and the Sanctum will be pretty safe. :P<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> my offer still stands, my fellow Awakened.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> do you have any prerequisites I must fulfill before my char can have his occult store?<br /> <br /> As for the Cabal, would you guys want a more central place, or outskirty? Sorry if I'm being annoying, but I get really giddy when building houses and I like to have a mapped out representation of my character's hangouts :P so, drawing up his shop is kinda a must for me, and the cabal place too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:14:51-07:00","id":1078617,"title":"","content":"You credit me with knowing what I am doing too much. I was going to save the experience. Now I am thinking about Fate 4. I don't see how to get to a Master. I do like playing a lucky character. How do you overload a skill? I am putting most of my points, 11 in social skills. Probably 3 at 3 and 1 at 2. I like to create situations that are in my favor, though in truth I am a noob. I just think Fate is really cool. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11807_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11807\" data-vbnamecard=\"11807\">HTaiji</a> I am in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 04-14-2017, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:27:06-07:00","id":1078622,"title":"","content":"I am not accusing anyone of anything, all I am saying is that I have seen players take 20 points and put Gnosis up to 5, Fate up to 5, 0 Merits and one skill in each category up to 5. Serendipity to change skill points around, Shifting the Odds to gain Merits to burn, drop the spell and then cast it again to gain different merits to use up and ditch. Now the game supports that kind of thing so it is allowed but just to say there are alot of ways around that and I know most of them.<br /> <br /> Overloading skills is putting one skill up to 5 in each category and the shifting the points around with Serendipity.<br /> <br /> Like I said Gnosis and Arcanum is limited to max of 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 04-14-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:33:36-07:00","id":1078629,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11807_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11807\" data-vbnamecard=\"11807\">HTaiji</a> I don't know Phoenix but my character would place a high value on being near Arizona State University. So probably a downtown sanctum would be best for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:48:10-07:00","id":1078636,"title":"","content":"My Gnosis will be 3 and my Fate will be 4 if I can get it. I am not liking the supercharge one stat and all. I did not get the trick with Serendipity before, now I respect the spell more. To get to 3 in Gnosis I need to use all my merit points. To get to 4 in Fate, I need all the 20 exp. Unless I am missing something, which I probably am, I don't even see a way to get 4 in Gnosis and 4 in Fate. Maybe I can get some advice from you in building this character.<br /> <br /> I want a fortuneteller writer. One of his social skills will be writing. He spends money as soon as he gets it. He uses magic to keep afloat. His merits are transient. The more I think about Fate 4 the more I want it. But I need Gnosis 3 and that requires sacrificing all of my merit points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3MaDlLEDWYsTmVsVGlEcjI2QkE/view?ths=true\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3MaDlLEDWYsTmVsVGlEcjI2QkE/view?ths=true\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3MaDlLEDWYsTmVsVGlEcjI2QkE/view?ths=true\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3MaDlLEDWYsTmVsVGlEcjI2QkE/view?ths=true </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","user":"wtaylorjr2001","date":". 04-14-2017, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:53:48-07:00","id":1078637,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> I think X per dot, in this system, means you pay X to raise a trait by one, not X times the number of dots, like in some other WW games.<br /> P.S. someone correct me if I'm wrong<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> How do you feel about legacies? I ask because I like the idea of my character founding their own legacy. I've been working on a homebrew but I'm new to the system and might not be able to tell if something is over powered (or under powered). I'm not even finished the first draft yet so if you say no to the whole idea that's fine. It's just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","user":"Fictional Dynasty","date":". 04-14-2017, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty","name":"Fictional Dynasty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:06:36-07:00","id":1078643,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> Acanthus starts with Time and Fate as Ruling. You start with 6 dots in Arcanum. Putting 3 in fate and 3 in time you would need to spend 4 experience to take fate to 4, and additional to take it to 5. That would be 8 points for a 5 Fate. Gnosis starts at 1 10 merit dots to take it to 3, 5 experience to take it to 4 and an additional 5 to take it to 5 gnosis. that is 10 points. So for 18 points you can have a 5 Gnosis and 5 Fate with 2 experience left over.<br /> <br /> If you start with a 3 in fate (3 of your starting 6) and spend 4 experience you will have a 4 Fate.if you spend 10 of the Experience point you can have a 3 Gnosis. That is without spending any of the starting merits on Gnosis. You would still have 6 points left over.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1081-fictional-dynasty\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1081_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1081\" data-vbnamecard=\"1081\">Fictional Dynasty</a> Legacies are fine and if you are starting your own the you need to develop the legacy. I can help with the legacy if you tell me about it.<br /> <br /> To all. There are alot of conversions of the Legacies in the Mage section, if you are using one from there link to it and I will check it out to see if it is one that I agree with. If you need on converted just say which one and I will look for one or help you convert it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:06:36-07:00","id":1078644,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> you can now buy the 4th dot of Fate for 4xp and you still have 16xp leftover for Merits. (Hardwire gave us 20xp each) If I may give you an advice, get a few dots of Dream. Would you be willing to give 2xp for 1 dot each of Safe Place and Sanctum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:13:16-07:00","id":1078649,"title":"","content":"ASU is in downtown Tempe, part of the Metro Phoenix area but it is it's own city. If that is where you want to be based that is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","da